      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\n`tests/quantization/test_cutlass_w4a16.py` guards its module-level skip with `has_device_capability(90)`, a `>=` test, so the Hopper-only Machete tests are collected on every newer architecture and fail. Switch to `is_device_capability(90)`, which is what the file's own docstring and skip message already describe.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Machete W4A16 tests skip on non-Hopper CUDA GPUs, as `\"Machete W4A16 requires Hopper (sm_90).\"` already claims.\n- Hopper is unchanged: `is_device_capability(90)` is `True` on sm_90, so the module is still collected there. Pre-Hopper GPUs were already skipped under both forms, and the `is_rocm()` branch is untouched.\n- Test-only change, one word.\n\n## Validation\n\nRan the file on GB300 (capability 103) before and after the change, in the same container (vLLM `0.31.0`):\n\n| | `pytest -q tests/quantization/test_cutlass_w4a16.py` |\n|---|---|\n| main | `8 failed, 1 passed in 49.09s` |\n| this PR | `1 skipped in 0.03s` — `SKIPPED [1] quantization/test_cutlass_w4a16.py:18: Machete W4A16 requires Hopper (sm_90).` |\n\nPredicate values measured on that device:\n\n| predicate | value |\n|---|---|\n| `get_device_capability()` | `103` |\n| `has_device_capability(90)` | `True` — current guard lets the module through |\n| `is_device_capability(90)` | `False` |\n\n## Details\n\n**Root cause.**\n\n1. Machete is built on `wgmma` PTX and is sm_90-only. The module says so twice: the docstring (`\"Tests for Cutlass W4A16 (Machete) kernel on Hopper\"`) and the skip message.\n2. The guard uses `has_device_capability(90)`, which is `>=`, so any capability above 90 passes it and the module is collected.\n3. On Blackwell `choose_mp_linear_kernel` correctly returns `MarlinLinearKernel`, so every assertion expecting `MacheteLinearKernel` fails. The product behaviour is right; only the guard is wrong.\n\n**Fix.** `is_device_capability(90)` matches sm_90 exactly, aligning the guard with the message.\n\n**Why CI did not catch this.** `.buildkite/test_areas/quantization.yaml` pins `tests/quantization/` to `device: h200_35gb`; only `test_blackwell_moe.py` runs on B200. No Blackwell runner collects this file today, so the validation above was performed outside CI.\n\nNot a duplicate: searched open and closed PRs for `test_cutlass_w4a16`, and for `machete` together with `is_device_capability`; nothing related. Upstream `main` still carries the original line.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR. Claude Code drafted it from a QA triage investigation; @ziruil-re is reviewing it before it leaves draft.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
